  "content": {
    "id": "p18-q26-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "26",
    "prompt": "Find the least multiple of 7 that when divided by 6, 9, 15, and 18, leaves 4 as the remainder in each case.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$364$\n\nSubtract 4 to obtain a common multiple of the four divisors, then find the first resulting number divisible by 7.",
      "worked": "Subtracting 4 gives a common multiple of 6, 9, 15 and 18.\n\n$$6=2\\times3,\\quad9=3^2,\\quad15=3\\times5,\\quad18=2\\times3^2.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\operatorname{LCM}(6,9,15,18)&=2\\times3^2\\times5\\\\\\operatorname{LCM}(6,9,15,18)&=90.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe possible numbers, in increasing order, are $4,94,184,274,364,\\ldots$. The first four are not divisible by 7, while $364=7\\times52$. Therefore, the least required multiple is $364$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
